question.en:
Classifying household waste is not only a current trend but also a necessity for ecological and environmental protection. Currently, a certain city generates around 900 tons of household waste every day. After sorting, excluding recyclable waste and waste needing special treatment, there are still about 800 tons of waste that need processing. To handle this waste, the city plans to build a waste incineration power plant that can burn 800 tons of household waste daily to generate electricity. Through experimental tests, it is found that the complete combustion of [X] household waste generates heat, with 30% of it being convertible into 9×10^8J of electrical energy. Find:  
The calorific value q of household waste;  
(Supplement: the mass of household waste is [X];) the specific heat capacity value of water is 4.2×10^3 J/(kg·℃). If we already know the answer to the above question is 3×10^6 J/kg, what should the content corresponding to [X] be in the question?

With the development of the national economy, cars have become part of every household. A car travels 100 km at a constant speed on a straight road, consuming gasoline [X]. If 30% of the heat released by the complete combustion of this gasoline is used to do useful work in driving the car, (q_{gasoline}=4.6×10^7J/kg, \rho_{gasoline}=0.7×10^3kg/m^3, 1L=0.001m³), find: 
The heat released by the complete combustion of this gasoline; 
The specific heat capacity of water is 4.2×10^3 J/(kg·℃). If we already know that the answer to the above problem is 3.22×10^8 J, then what should the content corresponding to [X] in the problem be?

As people's living standards continue to improve, cars increasingly become part of ordinary families. A car using gasoline as fuel travels at a constant speed of [X] on a horizontal road, where the engine power is 20KW. If the car travels a distance of 10 km, with gasoline having a calorific value of q = 4.6×10^7 J/kg, and the car engine efficiency being 25%, find:
(1) The time of movement;
(2) The work done by the engine;
(3) The mass of gasoline consumed. The water temperature rise parameter is 10 ℃. If we already know the answer to the above question is 0.87 kg, what should be the content corresponding to [X] in the problem?

The nameplate of a certain electric water heater is shown in the table below. Now, fill the tank with water, and when the electric water heater is working normally, it heats the water from 20℃ to 60℃. Given that c_water=4.2×10^3J/(kg•℃), ignoring heat loss, find:
The heat absorbed by the water;
The mass of the water is [X] (Note: The specific heat capacity of water is 4.2×10³J/(kg·℃);) The calorific value of ethanol is 3.0×10^7 J/kg. If we already know the answer to the above question is 8.4×10^6 J, then what should the content corresponding to [X] in the question be?

At the beginning of the month, the electricity meter at Xiaoming's home reads 1269.5 kW·h, and at the end of the month, the dial reads. Find:
1. The time these electric energy can power a 500 W electrical appliance;
2. The electric energy consumed this month is [X] (Note: power is 0.5 kW; ) with an initial temperature value of 20 ℃. If we already know the answer to the above question is 400 h, what should the content corresponding to [X] be in the question?
